candles were obliterated in a magical explosion. (Everyone who has had 
the same experience, please raise their hands.  Uh huh, just what I 
thought. Nikolai, you don't have to be so eager).

Therefore, I suggest Yet Another New Idea: making candles. (last such 
suggestion according to Google groups is sep  1 2000) Such a YANI would 
require the following:
A beehive would be guaranteed on one of the levels containing the 
Wizard's tower. This beehive would guarantee containing 7 beeswax. All 
other beehives would have a chance of generating beeswax (white %).
The wizards tower would have one room which would  contain at least 8 
lichens and 2 yellow fungi.
In order to create a beeswax candle, one would have to weild a lichen 
corpse in one hand, wield a beeswax in the other hand, and read a B/U 
scroll of light while hallucinating. (This is magic, don't ask what is 
holding the scroll). A wax candle would be created in the hand with the 
beeswax. The candle would be B/U depending on the state of the scroll of 
light.
If any one item is Blessed (scroll, beeswax, lichen) and any one other 
item is cursed, a magical explosion will occur; and you will lose d3 WIS 
(you idiot).

Cotton would be more realistic for the wick; but, coding to slice a 
t-shirt or robe into strips sounds unrealistic. Wool might be acceptable 
as a death drop for sheep; sheep would have to be added to the monster 
